{"data": [{"author_id": "2074691389640638464", "created_at": "2026-10-29T06:05:31.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115686449685405803"], "entities": {"hashtags": [{"end": 208, "start": 198, "tag": "AIServers"}, {"end": 219, "start": 209, "tag": "GPURepair"}, {"end": 225, "start": 220, "tag": "H100"}, {"end": 231, "start": 226, "tag": "H200"}, {"end": 237, "start": 232, "tag": "A100"}, {"end": 249, "start": 238, "tag": "AIHardware"}, {"end": 261, "start": 250, "tag": "DataCenter"}, {"end": 277, "start": 262, "tag": "GPUMaintenance"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/YR5HjrcAvS", "end": 301, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/alexwang3lf/status/2115686449685405803/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2115686407574343681", "start": 278, "url": "https://t.co/YR5HjrcAvS"}]}, "id": "2115686449685405803", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 6, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "What should you do if your computing cluster encounters a failure? With extensive experience in GPU repair, we are ready to provide the support you need to keep your computing power up and running!\n#AIServers #GPURepair #H100 #H200 #A100 #AIHardware #DataCenter #GPUMaintenance https://t.co/YR5HjrcAvS", "url": "https://x.com/alexwang3lf/status/2115686449685405803"}, {"author_id": "1188410845140791296", "created_at": "2026-10-30T00:46:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115968426531491919"], "entities": {"cashtags": [{"end": 99, "start": 94, "tag": "NBIS"}, {"end": 234, "start": 229, "tag": "SPCX"}, {"end": 257, "start": 252, "tag": "CRWV"}]}, "id": "2115968426531491919", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 2, "impression_count": 3111, "like_count": 26, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 3, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "We wouldn’t be surprised to see GPU rental revenue reach $100bn per gigawatt a year.\n\nNebius ($NBIS) has already reported a short-term deal in the $40m–$50m per MW annualised range. That is $40bn–$50bn per GW. Likewise for Space $SPCX and others while $CRWV sold its long term", "url": "https://x.com/convequity/status/2115968426531491919"}, {"author_id": "1194822976069222401", "created_at": "2026-10-29T18:14:35.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115869925558673681"], "id": "2115869925558673681", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 68, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "We live in a Weird Time in GPUs.\n\nEveryone says there's a GPU shortage.\nMeanwhile, GPUs sit in racks waiting for power.\n\nChip companies want to be clouds.\nClouds want to be chip companies.\n\nHyperscalers are building their own AI chips.\nAnd still buying every NVIDIA GPU they can", "url": "https://x.com/waiting4ragi/status/2115869925558673681"}, {"author_id": "84841519", "created_at": "2026-10-29T22:35:15.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115935521666990323"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/0uwOz2ot1x", "end": 303, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/TechFieldDay/status/2115935521666990323/video/1", "media_key": "7_2115935474858565632", "start": 280, "url": "https://t.co/0uwOz2ot1x"}]}, "id": "2115935521666990323", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 212, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "The era of focusing solely on massive GPU training clusters is over—the real enterprise networking battlefield has officially shifted to distributed inference. \n\nFor this takeaway, Tom Hollingsworth discusses how disaggregated inference architectures are transforming data center https://t.co/0uwOz2ot1x", "url": "https://x.com/TechFieldDay/status/2115935521666990323"}, {"author_id": "19153682", "created_at": "2026-10-30T09:03:51.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116093716557381809"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 259, "id": "2974990371", "start": 244, "username": "skywalkersound"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/40rVMX0W4Y", "end": 301, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/guifav/status/2116093716557381809/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2116093709313859584", "start": 278, "url": "https://t.co/40rVMX0W4Y"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/40rVMX0W4Y", "end": 301, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/guifav/status/2116093716557381809/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2116093711205462016", "start": 278, "url": "https://t.co/40rVMX0W4Y"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/40rVMX0W4Y", "end": 301, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/guifav/status/2116093716557381809/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2116093713004756992", "start": 278, "url": "https://t.co/40rVMX0W4Y"}]}, "id": "2116093716557381809", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 20, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Skywalker Sound runs 200+ M4 Max Mac Studios, and at least 100 sit idle each night (team estimate). The ML team turned 24 of them into a PyTorch training cluster over 10 Gb Ethernet, with the same training script the team uses on NVIDIA GPUs.\n\n@skywalkersound built MCCL (Metal https://t.co/40rVMX0W4Y", "url": "https://x.com/guifav/status/2116093716557381809"}, {"author_id": "2086152374263947265", "created_at": "2026-10-30T17:06:19.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116215133680623643"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/togethercomput…", "end": 235, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/togethercompute/status/2116214655106326879", "start": 212, "url": "https://t.co/iYJsCD73tw"}]}, "id": "2116215133680623643", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 4, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2116214655106326879", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Multi-turn tool use makes RL rollouts brutal because async generation kills GPU cluster throughput. Offloading rollout and training infra while letting teams bring custom environments removes a huge bottleneck.\n\nhttps://t.co/iYJsCD73tw", "url": "https://x.com/techwithjoe_io/status/2116215133680623643"}, {"author_id": "1879267728256872449", "created_at": "2026-10-29T19:36:56.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115890647764742379"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/iPAXQ0LIxp", "end": 304, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/HorizonWind2004/status/2115890647764742379/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2115887573834797056", "start": 281, "url": "https://t.co/iPAXQ0LIxp"}]}, "id": "2115890647764742379", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 12, "impression_count": 7730, "like_count": 49, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 15, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "Blindly trusting a coding agent is a mistake...\n\nI've been doing some vibe research on a remote GPU cluster lately. Claude kept telling me my research idea wouldn't work.\n\nI asked if the implementation matched the upstream code. It confidently said yes.\n\nThen I opened W&amp;B and https://t.co/iPAXQ0LIxp", "url": "https://x.com/HorizonWind2004/status/2115890647764742379"}, {"author_id": "2346869798", "created_at": "2026-10-30T19:28:37.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116250941057896909"], "entities": {"hashtags": [{"end": 154, "start": 149, "tag": "SC26"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/99dmoQfL9g", "end": 298, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/Quobyte/status/2116250941057896909/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2116250937677283328", "start": 275, "url": "https://t.co/99dmoQfL9g"}]}, "id": "2116250941057896909", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 8, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Your GPUs are only as fast as the storage feeding them.\n\nFrom training to agentic inference, storage decides how much work your GPUs actually do. At #SC26 in Chicago, see how Quobyte, Storage Architected for AI™, keeps them fed:\n- GPU-converged storage that runs on your GPU https://t.co/99dmoQfL9g", "url": "https://x.com/Quobyte/status/2116250941057896909"}, {"author_id": "1233216503626924033", "created_at": "2026-10-30T15:09:57.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116185846361796823"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/river_ai_inc/s…", "end": 302, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/river_ai_inc/status/2116183349056229407", "start": 279, "url": "https://t.co/rjd3oOov39"}]}, "id": "2116185846361796823", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 10, "impression_count": 4859, "like_count": 49, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 3}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2116183349056229407", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "The River API now supports training LLMs with any loss function. You define a custom loss in PyTorch on your laptop and we efficiently execute it at scale on our remote GPU cluster with zero overhead.\n\nThe blog explains how it works: the loss function is traced on your machine, https://t.co/rjd3oOov39", "url": "https://x.com/ibab/status/2116185846361796823"}, {"author_id": "2115672486767693824", "created_at": "2026-10-29T20:00:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115896452450771126"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "Explore PyTorch 2.15, featuring a rewritten NCCL backend by default, NVGEMM decode improvements, FP8 on Apple Silicon, and expanded platform support.", "display_url": "pytorch.org/blog/pytorch-2…", "end": 267, "expanded_url": "https://pytorch.org/blog/pytorch-2-15-release-blog/", "images": [{"height": 628, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2115500780749033472/i5voVjQH?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1200}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2115500780749033472/i5voVjQH?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 244, "status": 200, "title": "PyTorch 2.15 Release Blog - PyTorch", "unwound_url": "https://pytorch.org/blog/pytorch-2-15-release-blog/", "url": "https://t.co/u4BPKGSYwD"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/MNLu7IhLJe", "end": 291, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/Alanogrok/status/2115896452450771126/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2115882726306025472", "start": 268, "url": "https://t.co/MNLu7IhLJe"}]}, "id": "2115896452450771126", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 4, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "PyTorch 2.15 makes its rewritten NCCL backend the default, with flight-recorder dumps when a collective hangs.\n\nAt cluster scale, time spent finding a stalled rank belongs in the training budget. Diagnosis costs GPU-hours too.\n\nImage: PyTorch.\nhttps://t.co/u4BPKGSYwD https://t.co/MNLu7IhLJe", "url": "https://x.com/Alanogrok/status/2115896452450771126"}, {"author_id": "703823975646830604", "created_at": "2026-10-29T05:31:13.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115677817820368896"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/EAfOp8g7yZ", "end": 299, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/baremetalbalak/status/2115677817820368896/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2115677790276337664", "start": 276, "url": "https://t.co/EAfOp8g7yZ"}]}, "id": "2115677817820368896", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 7, "impression_count": 1572, "like_count": 17, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 3, "retweet_count": 2}, "text": "B200 capacity on io[.]net from USD 3.35/GPU-hr. 128 nodes, 1,024 GPUs, United States.\n\nPricing options:\n• 36 months: USD 3.35/GPU-hr, 50% upfront\n• 48 months: USD 3.75/GPU-hr, 25% upfront\n• 36 months: USD 3.85/GPU-hr, 25% upfront\n\nThe upfront payment is credited back against https://t.co/EAfOp8g7yZ", "url": "https://x.com/baremetalbalak/status/2115677817820368896"}, {"author_id": "442390892", "created_at": "2026-10-30T16:26:07.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116205014347903387"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/cLi9UpLqOl", "end": 299, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/Richdegen67/status/2116205014347903387/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2116205006856826880", "start": 276, "url": "https://t.co/cLi9UpLqOl"}]}, "id": "2116205014347903387", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 101223, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "🌐 SECURING DECENTRALIZED COMPUTE CLUSTERS ON TRON WITH WINKLINK DePIN TELEMETRY\n\nDecentralized GPU compute networks enable artificial intelligence developers to rent compute clusters for training neural network models using cryptocurrency payments. DePIN networks deployed on https://t.co/cLi9UpLqOl", "url": "https://x.com/Richdegen67/status/2116205014347903387"}, {"author_id": "1814538500915798016", "created_at": "2026-10-30T05:03:16.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116033171636855186"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/WIpStGCGWZ", "end": 304, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/openlabx_/status/2116033171636855186/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2116033123519762432", "start": 281, "url": "https://t.co/WIpStGCGWZ"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/WIpStGCGWZ", "end": 304, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/openlabx_/status/2116033171636855186/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2116033163801894912", "start": 281, "url": "https://t.co/WIpStGCGWZ"}]}, "id": "2116033171636855186", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 130, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "A 9,600 GPUs AI Supercomputer listed on Ebay for $59.7M :\n\n- Listed by Minnesota-based IT reseller Core 4 Solutions, the decommissioned cluster consists of 300 server racks, each packing 32 NVIDIA A100 40GB GPUs.\n\n- The full system includes 4,200 AMD EPYC Rome processors, 268,800 https://t.co/WIpStGCGWZ", "url": "https://x.com/openlabx_/status/2116033171636855186"}, {"author_id": "1920651001327202304", "created_at": "2026-10-28T21:27:32.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115556093279801830"], "id": "2115556093279801830", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 30, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "There was a time where your family owning a personal computer at home gave you an unmatched leg up against your peers, completely reshaping the trajectory of your life (young Mark Zuckerberg opportunity). There really hasn't been any technology since then that could give a kid", "url": "https://x.com/ryanhuos/status/2115556093279801830"}, {"article": {"title": "Why I’m not building a Neocloud"}, "author_id": "2034130498445041664", "created_at": "2026-10-29T13:33:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115799063085928883"], "entities": {"hashtags": [{"end": 210, "start": 193, "tag": "AIInfrastructure"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/i/article/2115…", "end": 234, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/i/article/2115796531961888768", "start": 211, "status": 404, "unwound_url": "https://x.com/i/article/2115796531961888768", "url": "https://t.co/fyaTHtcNlS"}]}, "id": "2115799063085928883", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 936, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 2, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "The GPU cloud isn’t broken. Its capital structure is.\n\nOur CEO Davy Wang on why GoodVision AI isn’t building a Neocloud, and the three lessons from the first cloud war that shaped our model. \n\n#AIInfrastructure https://t.co/fyaTHtcNlS", "url": "https://x.com/GoodVisionAI/status/2115799063085928883"}, {"author_id": "1500129839583567875", "created_at": "2026-10-29T05:47:52.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115682004989567011"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/PyTorch/status…", "end": 303, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/PyTorch/status/2115501310233456900", "start": 280, "url": "https://t.co/mXjhMK00VT"}]}, "id": "2115682004989567011", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 60, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2115501310233456900", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "After upgrading to PyTorch 2.15, every distributed NCCL training job runs on a new backend, and Macs on macOS 14 lose GPU acceleration.\n\nThe release, out yesterday, packs 3,117 commits from 583 contributors. The rewritten NCCL backend, opt-in as nccl2 in 2.14, is now the default https://t.co/